<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Damaji Rao Gaekwad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1768">1768</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Damaji Rao II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Damaji Rao Gaekwad was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> commander and ruler, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pilaji-rao-gaekwad">Pilaji Rao Gaekwad</a>, who led the family from 1732 to 1768. He took Baroda (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vadodara">Vadodara</a>) and much of Mughal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, making the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaekwads">Gaekwads</a> one of the great Maratha houses. He fought at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-battle-of-panipat">Third Battle of Panipat</a> in 1761 and survived the defeat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/damaji-rao-gaekwad.jpg" alt="Damaji Rao Gaekwad" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Damaji_Rao_Gaekwad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
